{"type": "say", "text": "Thanks, Morgan. I support all four adjustments — the minimum of 18 nodes directly addresses the latency breach I measured, and the other constraints from Casey, Taylor, and Jordan are all compatible with that. I'll file the latency measurement formally right after this meeting so it's tracked. One thing I want to confirm: with the minimum raised to 18 and maximum capped at 24, we have a narrower scaling band (18–24) than before (10–30). That's only 6 nodes of headroom for autoscaling during bursts. Based on my replay data, 18 nodes keeps us under the 300ms target, but I want to flag that we should monitor closely during the Monday traffic cycle to make sure 24 is sufficient headroom — if latency starts climbing near the upper bound, we may need to revisit the finance cap with Casey. Otherwise, I'm good with the policy as stated."}
```

